<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  Built-in oxygen for the Shipcracker helmet under Vanilla Gravship Expanded.

  VacuumResistance.xml (same root) drops the set to VGE1's 0.97 total so it obeys
  VGE1's rule that a suit alone never reaches full immunity. This patch gives the
  helmet the same comp VGE1's astrorig and oxygen packs use
  (VanillaGravshipExpanded.CompApparelOxygenProvider): while it holds oxygen and
  the wearer's base resistance is at least minResistanceToActivate, VGE1's
  StatPart_OxygenPack on VacuumResistance forces the wearer to 1.0. The stat part
  scans every worn apparel for the comp, so a helmet works as well as a belt pack.
  Numbers: 50 charges (half the astrorig's 100; a helmet-sized tank, about 1.6
  days of continuous vacuum at the comp's 1 charge per 2000 ticks), refilled 1
  oxygen canister per charge, auto-refill at a third like the astrorig.

  The comp requires tickerType Normal (a config error otherwise); VFEP's
  VFEP_WarcasketPartBase sets Never, so the child declares Normal here. Our def
  has no comps node of its own (the base carries Forbiddable and Colorable), so
  the whole node is added; child lists append to the parent's on inheritance.
  The chargeNoun is a new DefInjected point that lives in this root's Languages
  when translations land, never in the main tree.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="SCWC_WarcasketHelmet_Shipcracker"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <tickerType>Normal</tickerType>
      <comps>
        <li Class="VanillaGravshipExpanded.CompProperties_ApparelOxygenProvider">
          <maxCharges>50</maxCharges>
          <percentageToAutoRefill>0.334</percentageToAutoRefill>
          <fuelDef>VGE_OxygenCanister</fuelDef>
          <fuelCountPerCharge>1</fuelCountPerCharge>
          <destroyOnEmpty>false</destroyOnEmpty>
          <chargeNoun>oxygen u³</chargeNoun>
          <minResistanceToActivate>0.12</minResistanceToActivate>
        </li>
      </comps>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
